            "B": "Research an incremental exact verifier for the existing Heap permutation sequence. After each swap, update only the adjacency comparisons involving the changed source positions, maintaining the same result as the current full verifier. Cover diagonal entries and every unordered pair, and preserve the reference's permutation order and output behavior. Compare against full verification on varied valid graphs before proposing it.",
            "C": "Research a lossless, order-preserving pruning of Heap's permutation enumeration. A recursive form may skip a whole subtree only when a necessary partial-isomorphism constraint proves that no permutation in it can match. First establish byte-for-byte equivalence of the unpruned generator to the current sequence; verify pruning against exhaustive enumeration on small varied graphs. If output order or completeness cannot be guaranteed, do not use this approach.",
            "G": "Integrate only candidates with measured, correct end-to-end gains; measure combinations independently rather than assuming additive speedups. The baseline is correct on 4 cases at mean 0.0084209 s (score 0.5); this is limited evidence and gives no per-case timings or sizes. Target is ARM64 with 4 CPU cores, so account for overhead and do not add parallelism without measured benefit. Preserve exact reference output: notably, the source returns after printing identity if it matches, but otherwise continues Heap enumeration and prints every matching permutation. Do not replace that behavior with a single mapping or stop at the first non-identity match.",
