            "B": "Own per-state move-generation costs while retaining the same BFS semantics and exact state key. The source scans all boxes for occupancy on each move and bubble-sorts box positions after every transition. Investigate building an occupancy map once per expanded state, then updating the moved box in canonical sorted order without quadratic sorting. Precomputed neighbor indices or bounds checks may be evaluated separately. Preserve all legal moves and handle board edges safely; measure the complete candidate, not just the transition routine.",
