          "plan": {
            "A": "Research an exact-preserving top-k selection alternative to the per-point scan and array shifting, which costs O(P·k) for P points. A size-k max-heap is a candidate for O(P log k); retain each point’s original traversal ordinal so equal distances keep the same earlier-point preference as the source’s strict comparison. Preserve the distance calculation and verify vote tie-breaking against the source. Compare against the array approach across general k/P regimes; do not tune to particular test values. Report correctness and same-harness timings, not theoretical gains alone.",
            "B": "Research CPU parallelization suited to the ARM64 4-core target. After any sequential input parsing, distribute indexed points across workers, use private top-k state, and merge candidates with original traversal ordinals so equal-distance selection matches the source. Avoid shared per-point insertion or voting; measure whether thread and merge overhead is worthwhile. Use only the existing permitted toolchain/configuration, preserve the distance calculation and output semantics, and report correctness plus repeated end-to-end timings.",
