            "analysis": "This preparation concerns Problem A, KNN. For P=sum(group lengths), the supplied implementation scans up to k slots and may shift k entries per point, then sorts k labels; it allocates two k-sized arrays. Its baseline experiment is correct on the reported 4 cases, with the timings and score recorded for G above; this is the only performance evidence, not proof of correctness for every supported input or evidence that any proposed optimization helps. Preserve generic KNN computation and source-observable semantics, especially equal-distance selection order and plurality tie-breaking. All role ideas are hypotheses to measure; no candidate or integrated speedup is assumed."
