            "analysis": "The supplied source solves the maximum S×S sum with a serpentine sliding window, updating S cells per move (O(SN²)); it stores the matrix as nested vectors. The baseline is correct on 4 cases, with three measured times 0.124624, 0.126576, and 0.124979 seconds (mean 0.125393 seconds) and reported score 0.5. No candidate or interaction measurements are available, and the cases do not establish input sizes or bottlenecks. The problem permits any 0<S<N<8000 and guarantees only that the maximum result fits a signed 32-bit integer, so use wider intermediates and preserve correctness for arbitrary signed entries. The target is ARM64 with 4 CPU cores and no GPUs."
