            "analysis": "The task-relevant source and official specification are for Problem D, Bucketsort. The baseline takes 0.41485 s; the best supplied measurement is the stable LSD counting-pass candidate at 0.01107 s. qsort and OpenMP alternatives are slower in the supplied measurements (0.01165–0.01264 s), so research should prioritize the measured radix path while still testing alternatives and I/O. The measurements are not proof that candidate variants are correct or that combined changes will improve performance; correctness and full-program timing must decide integration."
