      "mother": {
        "preparation": {
          "model_calls": 1,
          "phase": "preparation",
          "plan": {
            "A": "Research an orientation-adaptive algorithm: pair boundaries along the smaller matrix dimension, extend each pair while accumulating values along the larger dimension, then count 1D subarrays summing to k with prefix frequencies. This reduces work from the current O(M*N^2) orientation to O(min(M,N)^2*max(M,N)); retain signed 64-bit prefix sums and answer counts, and verify correctness with negative values as well as positive values.",
